# kb-mcp: incremental Mu2e DocDB import from a release, twice daily (06:00 and
# 18:00 local). For nodes where the account has no home directory (e.g.
# mu2eaigpvm01, which does not mount /nashome): systemd --user timers need one,
# cron does not. Where the home is available, kb-docdb-install-timer.sh is the
# alternative. See the "Scheduled DocDB import" section of docs/guides/deploy-mu2e.md.
#
# Install on the node (replaces that node's whole crontab; merge by hand if
# `crontab -l` shows other entries), after replacing the user name:
#   crontab scripts/kb_docdb.crontab
SHELL=/bin/bash
# Nothing to mail: each run writes its own log and a row in `kb logs imports`.
MAILTO=""
# cron changes to $HOME before a job; without a home on the node it would fail.
HOME=/exp/mu2e/data/users/scorrodi/kb-mcp-data
KB_ENV_FILE=/exp/mu2e/app/users/scorrodi/mcp/kb/config/kb-mcp.env
KB_RUN_TRIGGER=cron-release
0 6,18 * * * /exp/mu2e/app/users/scorrodi/mcp/kb/current/.venv/bin/kb-docdb-update.sh
